      "side": 1,
      "message": "This assumes the EC CPU is little-endian, although it\u0027s confusing because I see `cbi_read_ufsc` treats the UFSC struct as a blob of bytes as well. Are the fields ever treated as 32-bit integers (the way they\u0027re declared), or is their interpretation also endianness-dependent (which seems bad)?",
      "range": {
